> What's a kid-friendly meal I can make with ground beef
**assistant**:
> How about making some homemade beef taco bowls? They're fun, customizable, and great for kids!
> 
> ### Ingredients:
> - 1 pound ground beef
> - 1 packet taco seasoning or your own mix (cumin, paprika, garlic powder, onion powder, and chili powder)
> - Taco shells or tortilla chips
> - Toppings: shredded lettuce, diced tomatoes, shredded cheese, sliced olives, sour cream, guacamole, salsa
> - Optional: black beans or corn
> 
> ### Instructions:
> 1. **Cook the Beef:** Heat a skillet over medium heat. Add the ground beef and cook until browned, breaking it up with a spoon as it cooks. Drain any excess fat.
> 2. **Season the Beef:** Add the taco seasoning and a bit of water according to the packet instructions (or a few tablespoons if using your mix). Stir to combine and let simmer for a few minutes.
> 3. **Prepare the Taco Bowls:** While the beef cooks, set up a toppings station. Divide the taco shells, lettuce, tomatoes, cheese, and other toppings into small bowls.
> 4. **Assemble:** Let the kids build their own taco bowls, starting with a base of beef and adding their choice of toppings. This can be a great way for them to express creativity and try new ingredients.
> 
> ### Tips:
> - Consider using lettuce leaves for a low-carb alternative to taco shells or chips.
> - Let your kids help with the setup and topping choices to make them more invested in the meal.
> 
> Enjoy the fun and interactive meal with your family!
